   "id": "sotah.21b.1",
   "daf": "21b",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "אוֹמֵר בֶּן עַזַּאי: חַיָּיב אָדָם לְלַמֵּד אֶת וְכוּ׳. רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר אוֹמֵר: כׇּל הַמְלַמֵּד אֶת בִּתּוֹ תּוֹרָה — מְלַמְּדָהּ תִּיפְלוּת. תִּיפְלוּת סָלְקָא דַּעְתָּךְ? אֶלָּא אֵימָא: כְּאִילּוּ לִמְּדָהּ תִּיפְלוּת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: From here «ben Azzai states: A person is obligated to teach» his daughter Torah, so that if she drinks and does not die immediately, she will know that some merit of hers has delayed her punishment. «Rabbi Eliezer says: Anyone who teaches his daughter Torah is teaching her promiscuity.» The Gemara asks: Could it «enter your mind» to say that teaching one’s daughter Torah is actually teaching her «promiscuity? Rather, say:» It is considered «as if he taught her promiscuity.»"
  }
 ],
